CM_ "Mazda Demio DY (2002-2007, JDM) / Mazda2 DY, ZJ-VE 1.3L with FN4A-EL 4AT.
Passive listen-only capture on the diagnostic CAN bus at 500 kbit/s.
Reverse engineered on one vehicle over 2026-08..2026-09; validated against
the factory instrument cluster, OBD-2 standard PIDs and GPS where possible.";

CM_ BO_ 560 "GEAR_RATIO is the MECHANICAL gear ratio, not the effective one.
It excludes torque converter slip: at a steady 3rd gear it stays at 1.00 while
the ratio computed from rpm and road speed spreads over 1.12..1.42.
The field is 8 bit, so ratios above 2.55 wrap: 1st (2.816) reads as 0.256 and
R (about 2.7) wraps as well. 2nd..4th are below 2.55 and never wrap.
Add 2.56 only for 1st and R - a naive 'below the mechanical ratio means it
wrapped' test misfires during shifts and produces ratios that do not exist.";

CM_ SG_ 560 GEAR "0x01..0x04 = 1st..4th, 0x10 = R, 0xF0 = N/P.";

CM_ SG_ 561 AT_RANGE "1=P 2=R 3=N 4=D 5=S 6=L.";

CM_ SG_ 1072 FUEL_LEVEL "Raw byte / 2.55, i.e. percent of sender span, not litres.
On this car about 0.45 L per point against fill-up receipts, with roughly 6%
spread; the sender clips at both ends and is not linear in between.
14.9 points was the reading when the factory low-fuel lamp came on.";

CM_ SG_ 1072 UNKNOWN_B1 "Not identified. Tracks battery voltage but is not the
voltage itself, and is not independent of FUEL_LEVEL: B0 + 2*B1 is about 418.
Use OBD-2 standard PID 0x42 for control module voltage instead.";

CM_ SG_ 1056 DISTANCE_PULSE "Free running 8 bit counter that increments with
distance travelled. Integrating it tracks GPS distance to about 0.1% over
80 km. Wraps; take differences modulo 256.";

CM_ SG_ 513 SPEED "Raw value is offset by 10000 and scaled by 100.
WHEEL_SPEEDS (0x4B0) uses the same encoding.";

VAL_ 560 GEAR 1 "1st" 2 "2nd" 3 "3rd" 4 "4th" 16 "R" 240 "N_P" ;
VAL_ 561 AT_RANGE 1 "P" 2 "R" 3 "N" 4 "D" 5 "S" 6 "L" ;
